                        <!-- SUB-TAB 4: HOW-TO GUIDE -->
                        <StackPanel x:Name="SettingsSubHowTo" Visibility="Collapsed">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource GhCard}" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource AccentFlame}">
                                <StackPanel>
                                    <TextBlock Text="How to Use GH3-Sync — Quick Feature Guide" FontSize="17" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentFlameText}" Margin="0,0,0,10"/>

                                    <TextBlock Text="1. 1-Click Community Charts (Chorus Encore)" FontSize="14" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimary}" Margin="0,4,0,3"/>
                                    <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12.5" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" LineHeight="20" Margin="0,0,0,10">
                                        Open ONOGAMI Song Creator and type any song or artist into the Chorus Encore search box. Click "⚡ Install to GH3" to download, unpack, and compile directly into Guitar Hero III, or click "Use Chart" to pair a handcrafted chart with your own audio file. Use the "Classic 5-Fret GH3" toggle if you prefer converting Clone Hero purple open-strum bars into classic green notes.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Text="2. AI Song Creator, Non-Guitar Songs &amp; Audio Mix Modes" FontSize="14" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimary}" Margin="0,4,0,3"/>
                                    <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12.5" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" LineHeight="20" Margin="0,0,0,10">
                                        • Playable Instrument Focus: Keep "Auto (Smart Multi-Lead)" for most songs — it detects guitar-heavy rock automatically and switches to multi-lead (Guitar, Keys, Sax/Synth) for non-guitar tracks. You can also target Guitar, Keys/Synth/Sax, Groove Bassline, or Vocal Melody explicitly.&#x0a;
                                        • Game Audio Mix Mode: "Auto" chooses Isolated Lead Stem (mute-on-miss) for guitar-dominant rock and Studio Master (untouched original audio, zero stem artifacts) for non-guitar, jazz, pop, hip-hop, or live tracks. "Hybrid Blend" keeps studio clarity with soft ducking on misses.&#x0a;
                                        • Batch Queue &amp; Multi-Drop: Drag-and-drop multiple MP3/WAV/OGG files at once (or click "+ Add to Batch Queue") to queue several songs, then click Edit on any queued card to tweak BPM, Feel, Focus, or Audio Mode individually before compiling!
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Text="3. My Customs, Re-Charting, Packs &amp; Deletion" FontSize="14" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimary}" Margin="0,4,0,3"/>
                                    <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12.5" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" LineHeight="20" Margin="0,0,0,10">
                                        • Click "Re-Chart AI v2" on any locally created song to re-generate its chart with the latest AI engine (beat-grid lock, riff memory, HOPOs, chords, and Co-Op Bass).&#x0a;
                                        • Click "+ Lobby" to add songs to your multiplayer Lobby Setlist, then use "Export Lobby Pack" to share your entire playlist as one drag-and-drop .gh3pack file.&#x0a;
                                        • Deleting a song cleanly removes its chart PAK, soundbank FSB/DAT, and strips its entry from DATA\customs.pak.xen while automatically taking a Career Save backup first.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Text="4. P2P Multiplayer Sync, Temporary Sessions &amp; Guitar HUD" FontSize="14" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimary}" Margin="0,4,0,3"/>
                                    <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12.5" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" LineHeight="20" Margin="0,0,0,10">
                                        Add friends via Friend Code in Friends &amp; Trust, then open P2P Sync &amp; Lobby to sync missing Lobby Setlist songs automatically. Enable "Temporary Session Mode" to borrow friends' songs for one play session and auto-clean them when GH3 exits (click "Keep Song" on any track you want to keep permanently). While playing GH3, the Electric Guitar HUD glows blue when connected and silver when offline.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Text="5. Career Saves &amp; First-Time Custom Setup" FontSize="14" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimary}" Margin="0,4,0,3"/>
                                    <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12.5" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" LineHeight="20">
                                        Adding your first custom song to a vanilla GH3 profile updates DATA\customs.pak.xen, triggering a one-time save reset in-game. After that initial custom profile is created, new songs merge cleanly without resetting your career. Paired Career Save snapshots back up both your save file and matching customs.pak.xen together.
                                    </TextBlock>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </Border>
